    {
      "id": 8995,
      "name": "phantaskippy",
      "username": "phantaskippy",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-11-10T20:21:08.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I was wondering how people play negative HP when targets are not indestructible.</p><p>A minion with 1hp is damaged for 5 hp, do they:</p><p>1) take 5 damage, drop to -4 HP and then are destroyed?</p><p>2) take 1 damage, drop to 0hp and then are destroyed?</p><p>This is important for AZ and Thermal Shockwave, but even for Fanatic (since she can Martyr herself to death if she has Aegis).</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The original ruling that involves the idea of negative HP was in response to Fixed Point, and it reads:</p><blockquote><p><span>Certain specific situations can make you go into negative HP temporarily and perhaps recover.</span></p></blockquote><p>I therefore play it that only when a target is indestructible can they enter negative HP.</p><p>But does hitting 0hp actually stop any more damage from being dealt? &nbsp;Or can you overkill and get benefit for it?</p><p>If Fanatic has 1hp and Aegis, can she drop herself into negative HP before recovering to 10, or can she only take 1 damage?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:39:40.039Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 2,
      "reads": 1,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 10.2,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 8992,
      "topic_slug": "negative-hit-points",
