      "can_see_hidden_post": false,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>I was wondering how people play negative HP when targets are not indestructible.</p><p>A minion with 1hp is damaged for 5 hp, do they:</p><p>1) take 5 damage, drop to -4 HP and then are destroyed?</p><p>2) take 1 damage, drop to 0hp and then are destroyed?</p><p>This is important for AZ and Thermal Shockwave, but even for Fanatic (since she can Martyr herself to death if she has Aegis).</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The original ruling that involves the idea of negative HP was in response to Fixed Point, and it reads:</p><blockquote><p><span style=\"font-family: verdana, 'lucida grande', arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; line-height: 14px; background-color: rgb(245, 245, 255);\">Certain specific situations can make you go into negative HP temporarily and perhaps recover.</span></p></blockquote><p>I therefore play it that only when a target is indestructible can they enter negative HP.</p><p>But does hitting 0hp actually stop any more damage from being dealt? &nbsp;Or can you overkill and get benefit for it?</p><p>If Fanatic has 1hp and Aegis, can she drop herself into negative HP before recovering to 10, or can she only take 1 damage?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
