    {
      "id": 81323,
      "name": "Envisioner",
      "username": "Envisioner",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2013-11-10T20:42:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I don't know of any official confirmation, but forum consensus seems to be that the amount of damage dealt is not constrained by the HP of the target, so Shockwave and Martyr both count overkill.&nbsp; Granted, the person who I remember most recently pointing this out was Foote, and I seem to recall you two tending to disagree on pretty much everything.&nbsp; But in general, the safest assumption seems to be that there are no \"invisible rules\" other than those in the Glossary (eg handling of duplicate Limited cards) or on the official website (eg shuffling your deck)...if you're mentally inserting a rule such as \"damage dealt to a target cannot exceed its current hit points\", where no such rule is explicitly stated, you're probably doing so in error.</p>",
      "post_number": 2,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:03:44.307Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 1,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.2,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 8992,
      "topic_slug": "negative-hit-points",
      "display_username": "Envisioner",
      "primary_group_name": null,
      "flair_name": null,
      "flair_url": null,
      "flair_bg_color": null,
